      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_634c0ac1f9616a15afb5d9d3a665cf8e7829c61d4563e49bc68d5c9fc658311c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The RMT correspondence is progressively calibrated across observables: GUE pair correlation models local zero spacings, high-zero computation tests that prediction, characteristic polynomials extend the model from locations to zeta-value moments, and family symmetry selects orthogonal, symplectic, or unitary Haar ensembles whose statistics predict moments, value distributions, and central vanishing. This breadth makes the model quantitatively testable without turning it into a proof of RH.",
