    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8cefbe8f633a6e284a763f04d8e48ad493e072a16bdfd2242f63fbd1bbc72905",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A possible Landau-Siegel zero is the common bottleneck behind several otherwise different methods. Excluding it would remove the ineffectivity in class-number control, while separate source-stated implications reduce that exclusion to crossing a fixed margin below the Brun-Titchmarsh constant 2, below one-half average zeta-zero spacing with the required recurring quantifier, or above one-half nonvanishing in a specified modular family. Across these methods, reaching the boundary is substantial but not enough.",
