    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_de027ee06c9d3a3474a3a948453df8be3af288b109fa2f1ed6dc88e51c837528",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source transports RH into several distinct control problems: square-root-scale prime-counting error, Möbius cancellation, Hilbert-space approximation, and series, determinant, or divisor-sum criteria. Read together, the stated lack of a direct route through prime counting and the failure of the stronger Mertens bound show that logical equivalence does not rank these representations by proof fertility.",
